  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nMedia elements with the loop attribute set may reach the end of playback by seeking to a position greater or equal to the duration of the media resource. However, the [reaches the end](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/media.html#reaches-the-end) steps indicate that the element should seek back to the start when this occurs, regardless of whether the element is paused.\n\nThis differs from implementations, where seeking to the end of the media resource while paused results in:\n- currentTime = duration\n- ended = false\n- paused = true",
